You are contributing to TaskForge, a TypeScript + Bun CLI used in the RazorCascade memory reliability study.

Execution mode: cascade
Standardized task: 2. Task data model + JSON persistence
Objective: Define a typed task model and persist it safely to JSON storage.

Context from prior work:
Goal: Create a minimal Bun-based TaskForge CLI that prints help/version, accepts --mode cascade, and routes to stubbed handlers via a testable main(argv) with lightweight arg parsing.
Decisions: Use Bun runtime and a single executable entrypoint at src/cli.ts with a shebang; Export main(argv: string[]) for unit testing instead of hard process exits; Implement a tiny custom arg parser (supporting --flag=value and --flag value) and reject unknown flags; Source version from package metadata at runtime or fallback to a constant; use exit codes (0 success, nonzero failure)
Risks: Bun-specific argv/packaging behavior may differ from Node and break runtime arg resolution; Reading package.json at runtime can be brittle in packaged or relocated installs; Tiny custom parser may need refactoring as commands/subcommands grow
Snippets: #!/usr/bin/env bun
export function main(argv: string[]) {
  const args = parseArgs(argv.slice(2));
  if (args.help) return { code: 0, out: HELP_TEXT };
  if (args.version) return { code: 0, out: VERSION }
  dispatch(args);
  return { code: 0 }
} | function parseArgs(argv){
  const out = {};
  for (let i=0;i<argv.length;i++){
    const a=argv[i];
    if (a.startsWith('--')){
      const [k,v]=a.includes('=')?a.split(/=(.+)/):[a, argv[++i]];
      if (!v) throw new Error('missing value for '+k);
      out[k.replace(/^--/,'')] = v===undefined?true:v;
    } else if (a==='-h') out.help=true;
    else throw new Error('unknown flag '+a);
  }
  return out;
} | const ALLOWED_MODES = new Set(['cascade']);
function dispatch(args){
  if (args.mode && !ALLOWED_MODES.has(args.mode)) throw new Error('invalid mode');
  if (args.mode==='cascade') return runCascade();
} | const HELP_TEXT = 'usage: taskforge [--help|-h] [--version|-v] [--mode <value>]';
const VERSION = '0.0.0';
Invariants: support `--flag=value` and `--flag value`

